The conversation focused on synthesizing complex information from a report for Ministries of Finance. Key messages emphasized the necessity of integrating climate risks into macroeconomic planning and investment. Participants highlighted the importance of building analytical capabilities to assess such risks and opportunities, leveraging diverse modeling approaches. Additionally, they discussed the need for a long-term vision for a climate-resilient economy, encouraging collaboration across government departments. Strategies for integrating adaptation into development planning and creating enabling conditions were outlined, including prioritizing early adaptation options and aligning national adaptation plans with budget processes. Lastly, the role of Finance Ministries in managing fiscal risks related to climate change, including stress-testing and debt management strategies, was underscored.
